==English==

===Etymology===
From English [[colre]], from Old French colre, from Latin [[cholera]], "[[jaundice]]", from {{etyl|grc}} [[kholera]], from [[khol]], "[[bile]]"

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|kō'lər}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# [[anger|Anger]] or [[irritability]].
# One of the [[w:four humours|four humours]] of ancient physiology, also known as [[yellow bile]].

====Synonyms====
* [[wrath]], [[rage]], [[fury]], [[passion]], [[ire]] [[gall]], [[anger]], [[indignation]], [[displeasure]], [[vexation]], [[grudge]], [[spleen]], [[bile]] or [[yellow bile]]

====Translations====
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|kiukku}}

